{% doc %}
  An event as a card, for rows that mix events with exhibitions (Home's What's on, DS-54): image,
  what it belongs to, title, when. The event's own image, else its exhibition's key image, else its
  programme page's hero image, so every card has a picture without anyone adding one twice.
  The whole card links to the event's own page when it has one (DS-176), else the exhibition,
  else the programme page, else the tickets.

  A line under the date names the exhibition ("Collect, Assemble, Gather") or the programme ("Music
  at the Smith"); an event titled like its programme ("Explore + Create") has none. It sits under
  the title, not above it, so every title in a row starts at the same height (DS-55). An event with
  both, such as a curator's tour listed on Professional development, is named and linked by its
  exhibition, which is what visitors know it by (DS-71).

  Beside the home hero, an event of the exhibition the hero leads with doesn't show the hero's
  picture again: when the hero shows that exhibition's key image (it has no installation views),
  the event's programme page hero comes before the key image (DS-95, Proposed).

  @param {object} event - An event entry
  @param {string} [heading] - Heading element for the title: 'h3' (default) or 'h2'
  @param {string} [lead] - The handle of the exhibition the home hero leads with (gs-lead-exhibition)

  @example
  {%- render 'gs-event-card', event: event -%}
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  assign tag = heading | default: 'h3'
  assign programme = event.programme_page.value
  assign exhibition = event.exhibition.value
  assign image = event.image.value
  assign mode = 'photo'
  # The hero already shows this exhibition's key image: the programme's picture comes first (DS-95).
  if image == blank and exhibition != blank and programme != blank and lead != blank
    if exhibition.system.handle == lead and exhibition.installation_views.value == blank
      assign image = programme.metafields.custom.hero_image.value
      if programme.metafields.custom.hero_is_artwork.value == true
        assign mode = 'artwork'
      endif
    endif
  endif
  if image == blank and exhibition != blank
    assign image = exhibition.key_image.value
    if exhibition.key_image_is_artwork.value == true
      assign mode = 'artwork'
    endif
  endif
  if image == blank and programme != blank
    assign image = programme.metafields.custom.hero_image.value
    if programme.metafields.custom.hero_is_artwork.value == true
      assign mode = 'artwork'
    endif
  endif

  assign label = ''
  if exhibition != blank
    assign label = exhibition.title.value
  elsif programme != blank
    assign a = programme.title | strip | downcase
    assign b = event.title.value | strip | downcase
    if a != b
      assign label = programme.title
    endif
  endif

  # An exhibition has a page when it has a summary or body, as gs-exhibition-card decides.
  assign ex_linked = false
  if exhibition != blank
    if exhibition.summary.value != blank or exhibition.body.value != blank
      assign ex_linked = true
    endif
  endif
  # An event with a page of its own links there (DS-176); else as before.
  capture own_page
    render 'gs-event-page-link', event: event
  endcapture
  assign own_page = own_page | strip
  assign href = ''
  assign by_tickets = false
  if own_page != blank
    assign href = own_page
  elsif ex_linked
    assign href = exhibition.system.url
  elsif programme != blank
    assign href = programme.url
  elsif event.tickets.value.url != blank
    assign by_tickets = true
  endif
-%}
<article class="gs-card">
  {%- if image != blank -%}
    {%- render 'gs-media', image: image, preset: 'card', mode: mode, ratio: 'var(--gs-ratio-card)' -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  <div class="gs-card__body">
    <{{ tag }} class="gs-card__title">
      {%- if by_tickets -%}
        {%- render 'gs-link', link: event.tickets.value, label: event.title.value -%}
      {%- elsif href != blank -%}
        <a href="{{ href }}">{{ event.title.value | escape }}</a>
      {%- else -%}
        {{- event.title.value | escape -}}
      {%- endif -%}
    </{{ tag }}>
    <p class="gs-status__dates"><time datetime="{{ event.starts.value }}">{% render 'gs-time-range', start: event.starts.value, end: event.ends.value %}</time></p>
    {%- if label != blank -%}
      <p class="gs-meta">{{ label | escape }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- render 'gs-data-event', event: event -%}
  </div>
</article>
